UID: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-GAP-SEMANTICS-LIVE-IN-TOOLS-WITH-NO-OWNER
TITLE: Semantics still live in tools with no owner
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
WIDGET: prose
PLACE: screen
STATEMENT: >>>
The readiness predicate, the fingerprint ripple, the signing gate, the plan-reference check and the layout rules are all semantic-layer rules written in Python. The node that records the misplacement has its judgement deliberately pending and no work node. And the lane rule — the one thing the ruling that decomposed SLICE into work ([LINK: DEC-SLICE-DECOMPOSES-TO-WORK]) gained — has no layer information to check against.

> Semantics still live in tools with no owner: readiness predicate, fp-check ripple, fp-accept gate, MECH-PLAN-REFS-CHECK and the layout rules are all L3 rules in Python (MECH-MILESTONE-TWO-SEMANTICS-MISPLACED pending, no WORK node), and DEC-DEFER-LAYER leaves the lane rule -- the one thing DEC-SLICE-DECOMPOSES-TO-WORK gained -- with no LAYER input to check against.
<<<
